@startuml
!define RECTANGLE class
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor #F0F0F0
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
title System Architecture: statlord - Real-time Display Data System

package "Client Layer" {
  [Browser Editor]
  [Viewer Component]
  [Display Devices]
}

package "Server Layer" {
  [Python/Django Server]
  [Static Assets Server]
  [API Endpoints]
}

package "Data Layer" {
  [PostgreSQL Database]
  [Data Entities]
}

package "External Systems" {
  [API Clients]
  [Build System]
}

' Core system components and relationships
Browser Editor -down-> [TypeScript/React SPA]
Browser Editor -down-> [Redux State Management]
Browser Editor -down-> [Canvas Editor]

Viewer Component -down-> [Display Renderer]
Viewer Component -down-> [Pixel Generator]

Display Devices -down-> [OLED Displays]
Display Devices -down-> [E-paper Displays] 
Display Devices -down-> [LCD Displays]
Display Devices -down-> [Browser Views]

Python/Django Server -down-> [API Controllers]
Python/Django Server -down-> [Data Models]
Python/Django Server -down-> [Business Logic]

Static Assets Server -down-> [Client Build Output]
Static Assets Server -down-> [Web Resources]

API Endpoints -down-> [Gauge API]
API Endpoints -down-> [Display API]
API Endpoints -down-> [Layout API]

PostgreSQL Database -down-> [Gauge Table]
PostgreSQL Database -down-> [Display Table]
PostgreSQL Database -down-> [Layout Table]

Data Entities -down-> [Gauge Entity]
Data Entities -down-> [Display Entity]
Data Entities -down-> [Layout Entity]

API Clients -down-> [Data Posting]
API Clients -down-> [Display Registration]

Build System -down-> [Node.js/npm]
Build System -down-> [Python 3.7+]

' Main data flows and interactions
Browser Editor --> Static Assets Server : Serves static files
Browser Editor --> API Endpoints : CRUD operations
Browser Editor --> Viewer Component : Render requests

Viewer Component --> API Endpoints : Fetch display data
Viewer Component --> Display Devices : Render output

API Clients --> API Endpoints : Post data / Register displays
API Endpoints --> Python/Django Server : Process requests
Python/Django Server --> PostgreSQL Database : Persist data
Python/Django Server --> Data Entities : Business logic

Build System --> Static Assets Server : Builds client assets
Static Assets Server --> Browser Editor : Serves application

' Component details and annotations
note top of [Browser Editor]
  TypeScript/React Single-Page Application
  Redux-managed state for:
  - Controls
  - Elements
  - Layouts
  - Gauges
  - Displays
  Canvas-based layout editing
end note

note top of [Python/Django Server]
  Python 3.7+ runtime
  Development server (runserver)
  API-backed data entities
  Containerized deployment
  Development-grade (not production-ready)
end note

note top of [Viewer Component]
  Display-oriented rendering path
  Black-and-white pixel generation
  Resolution-specific output
  Browser-based rendering
end note

note top of [PostgreSQL Database]
  Required for development
  Persists:
  - Gauge data (key, value)
  - Display records
  - Layout definitions
  Foreign key relationships
end note

note top of [API Endpoints]
  RESTful API for:
  - Gauge resources (key, value)
  - Display registration
  - Layout management
  Structured JSON payloads
end note

note top of [Display Devices]
  Multiple display types supported:
  - OLEDs
  - E-paper
  - LCDs
  - Browsers
  Unique identifiers
  Resolution metadata
  Rotation support
end note

' System boundaries
rectangle "Development Environment" {
  [Browser Editor]
  [Viewer Component]
  [Python/Django Server]
  [Static Assets Server]
  [PostgreSQL Database]
  [Build System]
}

rectangle "External Integration" {
  [API Clients]
  [Display Devices]
}

' Key relationships and dependencies
BuildSystem ..> Node.js/npm : requires
BuildSystem ..> Python 3.7+ : requires
Python/Django Server ..> PostgreSQL Database : depends on
Browser Editor ..> Static Assets Server : depends on
API Endpoints ..> Data Entities : manages

' Data model relationships
[Gauge Entity] --> [Gauge Table] : persists to
[Display Entity] --> [Display Table] : persists to
[Layout Entity] --> [Layout Table] : persists to

[Display Entity] --> [Layout Entity] : references (current_layout)
[Layout Entity] --> [Display Entity] : positions (display_positions)

@enduml